<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michigamea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Michigamea were an Algonquian-speaking people who belonged to the Illinois Confederation. When Marquette and Jolliet descended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> in 1673 they lived in what is now north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkansas">Arkansas</a>, and they later moved north to settle near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaskaskia">Kaskaskia</a> on the middle Mississippi. Weakened by war and disease, they merged with other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> peoples, whose descendants form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoria">Peoria</a> Tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/michigamea.jpg" alt="Michigamea" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Nikater · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illinois02.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
